From f8ff20e57ba6118389ce7055109a26886de28cdb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 20:01:33 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(credential-pool): rotate on the first 429 when the
 provider window exceeds a live wait [daveey]

Rate-limit recovery was "retry the same credential once, rotate on the second
429". With Anthropic's Retry-After: 600 that retry slept the whole 10-minute
window on a throttled key while a healthy sibling pool entry was available
(bb-worker job-a2a3529c / BB-87: silent 10 min, then rotated and answered in
2.5 s). When the 429's reset window (Retry-After / reset_at) is longer than
LIVE_RETRY_WAIT_CAP_S (60 s) the pool now rotates on the first 429; short or
unknown windows keep retry-once. A sole credential still reports no recovery,
so the fallback chain / wait run as before.

Fixes BB-87

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 agent/agent_runtime_helpers.py                |  28 ++-
 .../test_429_long_retry_after_rotates.py      | 172 ++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 197 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)
